n: 3.5
name: bml
kind: hub
is: BML names four things: the 2000 system (grammar language, language, abstract machine, object model; thesis unfinished, 21 not-supported marks) and three 2026 readers that give fail, choice, cut, class and template different meanings. 2000 choice is re-entrant on a machine that undoes; 2026 choice is scoped, or a first non-absent value over immutable data. Multiple inheritance by delegation and the (object, interface) reference pair have no running witness in either era. The reading read sources and ran nothing.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.1
name: scope
kind: hub
is: What the word BML covers and how the reading knows it: one 2000 system of four technologies whose thesis is unfinished, three 2026 readers with different meanings for the same words, and a study that read files and executed nothing.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.1.1
name: bml-2000-four-technologies
kind: observation
is: BML in 2000 is four technologies by two authors: BMF, a top-down backtracking parser definition language; BML, the language; BMA, the abstract machine; BMO, the object model. A seven-phase compiler targets an interpreting virtual machine; there is no native code generation and no unification.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#6 2.3.1#90 2.3.1#769-846 2.3.1#1011-1015 2.8.2#34-37 2.8.2#246
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.1.2
name: thesis-2000-unfinished
kind: observation
is: The 2000 thesis text is incomplete as a specification: the sections Overloading, Templates and Exception Handling hold one to three paragraphs each, Compatibility is an empty heading, the Conclusion is three empty headings, and 21 not-supported-yet marks stand in the attribute list.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#748-765 2.3.1#1018-1023 2.3.1#640-690
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.1.3
name: three-readers-2026
kind: observation
is: The 2026 body carries three BML readers: (a) a 135-line cursor grammar that erases types and bases and emits fail as a throw node; (b) a 4,400-line compiler for the thesis grammar with classes, delegation, templates and a field journal; (c) the form.bml dialect most of the body is written in, where fail and stop are the value nothing.
status: observed
src: 2.8.11#18-20 2.8.11#71-72 2.8.12#937-1012 2.8.13#1-13 2.8.14#52
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.1.4
name: study-executed-nothing
kind: finding
is: The BML study ran no BML or Form program and no 2000 binary, so every observation under hub 3.5 is a reading of source text or documents. Of the 490,522-byte thesis-lane compiler file the reading read the comments and about 200 lines.
status: assumed
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2
name: control
kind: hub
is: In 2000 choice is a re-entrant choice point on a machine that undoes everything not exempted, cut has two descriptions, and stop and timeout do not exist. In 2026 reader (b) scopes choice to its statement and journals field sets, and reader (c) reduces fail, stop and timeout to the value nothing over one recover point.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.1
name: choice-2000-sources
kind: observation
is: The 2000 thesis defines choice as code blocks tried in order, each run when the one before fails. Three 2000 sources place a failure after the completed statement: if_fail is defined as a choose followed by the failing statement, a test program has fail after its choose, and ChoiceSet.Pick returns another element on a later failure.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#625-626 2.3.1#927-932 2.8.2#58-66 2.8.2#1007-1008
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.2
name: choice-2000-is-re-entrant
kind: finding
is: Choice in the 2000 system is re-entrant: a failure raised after a choice statement has completed returns into the statement and runs its next branch.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.2.1 3.5.2.6
limit: Inferred from documents and source text. No 2000 program was run and the virtual machine's choice-point code was not read.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.3
name: choice-2026-two-meanings
kind: observation
is: In 2026 reader (b) choice is a statement that runs each branch from the state it was entered with and takes the first that ends unfailed; a later failure travels outward. In reader (c) choice is an expression that returns the first non-absent answer, zero included, and restores nothing; its grammar reads only the spelling choice.
status: observed
src: 2.8.13#525-531 2.8.12#1981-1988 2.8.18#104-106 2.8.16#691-696 2.1.13#35 2.8.14#269
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.4
name: fail-and-stop
kind: observation
is: In 2000 fail forces the machine into failure mode; the thesis has no stop word and leaves open what a program answers when no path is left. In 2026 reader (b) an unheld fail ends the program with the value of its last completed statement, in reader (c) fail and stop are both the value nothing, and the kernel's stop unwinds to the nearest attempt.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#633-634 2.3.1#245 2.8.28#9-17 2.8.18#173 2.8.14#52 2.1.13#26-30 2.8.23#33 2.1.7#362-367
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.5
name: cut-meanings
kind: observation
is: Cut in 2000 is a grammar primitive that, executed backwards, reports an error, undoes everything and stops, and also a statement that disables retries back to a matching mark. In 2026 reader (b) cut commits the enclosing choice to the current branch, with three cases pinned by a fixture, and in reader (c) cut offers only the first alternative.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#160-161 2.8.6#19 2.8.2#77-78 2.8.13#568-573 2.8.30#8-24 2.8.26#35-46 2.8.17#8
limit: How the two 2000 descriptions reconcile is not stated in what the reading read. The fixture was read, not run.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.6
name: undo-2000-machine-mode
kind: observation
is: In 2000 undo is the execution mode of the machine, not a statement: the machine state has a mode printed as UNDO or DO, a native method supplies a do, a redo and an undo function, and undoing reaches console output and object destruction. The attribute nostate exempts a variable or a stream; the thesis marks nostate not supported yet.
status: observed
src: 2.8.7#32 2.8.3#634 2.3.1#84 2.3.1#743 2.3.1#667 2.8.2#1014
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.7
name: undo-and-store-2026
kind: observation
is: 2026 reader (b): save, mark, restore and discard keep a stack of snapshots; a field set made while a snapshot is open is journaled and undone newest first; choice takes the same snapshot. Reader (c): store and restore are identity functions, undo selects the checkpoint when the acknowledgment is absent, and host effects are not rolled back.
status: observed
src: 2.8.12#1941-1948 2.8.12#2072-2087 2.8.13#715-718 2.8.31#12 2.8.32#11-12 2.8.17#16-18 2.8.18#176 2.8.18#367-368
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.8
name: timeout
kind: observation
is: 2000 has no timeout; the grammar primitive Multi match bounds retries, and speculation by one thread excludes all others. In 2026 timeout has no surface word, only a control tag for model streams: axiom 1 makes timeout nothing, the timeout walk counts attempts, not time, and reader (b) reads a run budget in milliseconds as an offer of more time.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#168-169 2.8.4#4 2.1.1#48 2.8.18#442-444 2.8.21#36 2.8.17#19-27 2.8.13#771-779
limit: Whether the 2000 machine enforced the retry bound is unknown: the BML source of Multi match only forwards the match.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.9
name: try-catch-throw
kind: observation
is: 2000 exceptions use a channel apart from failure: typed catch, jerr handler jumps, the termination model. 2026 reader (b) holds the thrown value in a cell, while reader (c) lowers try to an attempt, so its handler learns only that the body was absent; in its backtrack walk a node acknowledgment appends a payload to memory and the walk goes on.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#627-632 2.3.1#762 2.3.1#967-981 2.8.13#500-512 2.8.15#392-393 2.8.18#104-105 2.8.17#29-33
limit: The thesis does not say whether a throw undoes state; the reading looked and found no statement.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.2.10
name: reversible-machine-or-persistent-data
kind: finding
is: 2000 made the machine reversible and exempted what must persist. 2026 made most data immutable (reader (c)'s values, cursors, and reader (b)'s locals as lowered, one name per assignment), journals reader (b)'s field sets while a snapshot is open, and declares host effects not rolled back.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.2.6 3.5.2.7 3.5.4.3 1.3 1.7.8
src: 2.8.13#4 2.8.12#2084-2087 2.8.18#176 2.8.18#378-379
why: A reversible machine pays for undo on every instruction; an immutable value costs nothing to keep, and a host effect comes back only when the caller writes the saved value back.
limit: The per-instruction cost of the 2000 machine is argued from its design, not measured. That the 2000 machine loses nothing is not shown: the reading records as unknown how it undoes output to a real file or device. In its source text reader (b)'s locals are mutable and a snapshot saves and restores them.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3
name: objects
kind: hub
is: 2000 defines a reference as (object id, interface id, native flag) with two bases on every call, and multiple inheritance as one structural base plus delegation, marked unsupported in the thesis. 2026 reader (b) uses one record with a class id and one receiver, and no run of delegation or of the reference pair was seen in either era.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.1
name: templates-and-generics
kind: observation
is: 2000 templates are class and interface templates whose parameters are bounded by an interface, may be constants and may have defaults. 2026 reader (b) specializes by substitution, one class per type-argument list, without bounds; reader (c) declares templates without specialization and executes only comparison contracts as typing.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#755-757 2.8.12#4095-4100 2.8.33#13-15 2.8.20#32-33 2.8.18#504-505 2.8.18#187-205
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.2
name: classes
kind: observation
is: 2000: a class is a structural specification with a list of interfaces, and class-level data lives in a common object. 2026 reader (b): an object is one record carrying a class id and every field, with a method table that reads the class id; in reader (c) a class only groups functions, with no instances and no dispatch.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#234 2.8.3#660-662 2.8.13#598-602 2.8.18#504 2.8.14#114-116
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.3
name: multiple-inheritance
kind: observation
is: 2000: a class has one structural parent and each further parent becomes a delegated field; the attribute delegate is marked not supported yet. 2026 reader (b) reads the first super as structural and each later class super as a delegation base that lends methods and subtype, not fields; none of 9 class fixtures contains the word delegate.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#234 2.3.1#656 2.3.1#722-723 2.8.3#711 2.8.12#4254-4257 2.8.12#3363-3365 2.8.34#5-6 2.8.35 2.8.36
limit: The 248-line class-model test was not read in full and the 106-line core class surface was opened by no report. That delegation runs end to end is assumed for 2026 and unseen for 2000.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.4
name: reference-pair-2000
kind: observation
is: The 2000 object-model thesis defines a reference as object identifier, interface identifier and native flag, so two references to one object may carry different interfaces. Every method takes a behavioral base that dispatches and a structural base for field access; an interface cast pairs the found interface with the original structure.
status: observed
src: 2.8.3#486 2.8.3#493 2.8.3#642-644 2.8.3#649-651 2.8.5#103
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.5
name: pair-absent-in-2026
kind: finding
is: The 2026 thesis-lane lowering does not use the reference pair: an object is one record and an interface call compares the record's class id against table rows. A delegated call is re-invoked on the delegate field's value, which makes the delegate the receiver, so the 2000 rule that dispatch stays on the true object is not preserved.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.3.2 3.5.3.3 3.5.3.4
src: 2.8.13#604 2.8.13#632 2.8.13#684-685
limit: Read from three lines of the lowering. No case was run that would show it, such as a delegated method calling an overridden method.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.3.6
name: attributes
kind: observation
is: 2000 lets every definition carry attributes in seven contexts: class, inheritance, method, field, argument, variable, function. Of about 45 attributes tabulated, about 12 are honoured by 2026 reader (b), among them get, put, delegate, strict and the access levels; reader (b) carries and voices a flag to which the thesis gives no behaviour.
status: observed
src: 2.8.3#153 2.8.2#99-127 2.3.1#640-690 2.8.12#3554-3559 2.8.12#3593-3594 2.8.20#21
limit: An attribute listed as not found means the reading's search of comment lines showed no handling; it is not proof of absence.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.4
name: grammar-and-lowering
kind: hub
is: In 2000 grammar elements are objects that match and print themselves as grammar text, and the combinators are a few lines of choose and fail. In 2026 grammar is data over an immutable byte cursor with ordered alternatives and greedy repetition, and lowering passes through text: a 59,464-byte source becomes a 38,391,347-byte image.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.4.1
name: bmf-2000-grammar-is-objects
kind: observation
is: In 2000 BMF each grammar element is a class with Match, AsString (prints grammar text) and AsCreateString (prints the constructor call that rebuilds it). Rules take arguments, a method in a rule is a predicate whose failure sends the parser to another path, rules may change during a parse, and any object may carry text and binary syntaxes.
status: observed
src: 2.8.8#62-131 2.8.9#13-31 2.3.1#148-152 2.3.1#182 2.3.1#80-82 2.8.2#239
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.4.2
name: combinators-from-choose-and-fail
kind: observation
is: The 2000 source of Branch.Match is a loop over the items of choose { item.Match; return } , { } followed by fail, and Repeat.Match is a loop up to the maximum of choose { item.Match } , { if count < minimum fail; return }. The repeat behaviour the thesis describes, starting at the maximum and backing off one element, is coded in neither method.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#158
limit: Neither was run.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.4.3
name: bmf-2026-grammar-is-data
kind: observation
is: 2026 BMF keeps grammar as data: patterns and templates are lists, the cursor is an immutable byte position over a surface, alternatives are tried in order and never revisited, repetition is greedy, and a text rule may name an emit action and a reverse action. Not found: rules with arguments, grammar change during a parse, predicates inside rules.
status: observed
src: 2.8.24#19-21 2.8.24#433-441 2.8.24#512-518 2.8.25#817-826 2.8.27#235-236 2.8.22#9
limit: The 1,138-line grammar engine file was read in part, so not found is bounded by that reading.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.4.4
name: lowering-2026-through-text
kind: observation
is: The 2026 form.bml path is text to grammar templates to Form text to a C parse to node rows to a flat image; the lowering compiler runs as a cell inside the runtime's own process. A 59,464-byte source becomes 201,998 bytes of lowered text and a 38,391,347-byte image, 645 times its source, because a closure of 351 units is assembled whole.
status: observed
src: 2.8.19#5-12 2.1.7#33187-33194 2.8.29#1-14
limit: Measured by the old body on 2026-11-13 on one machine (cold build 12.94 s) and read from its document, not rerun. The reading says a child process over a pipe, as the compiler file's header still does; the runtime source has replaced that.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.5
name: ten-primitives
kind: finding
is: Ten primitives underlie everything BML expresses, none built from the others: a four-valued answer; a recover point; re-entry of a recover point; commit; state with a declared inverse; a reference as a (structure, behaviour) pair; a cursor over a surface; attributes on any declaration; parameterised declarations; identity independent of name.
status: inferred
conf: mid
