at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.6
name: derivable-constructs
kind: finding
is: Derivable from the ten primitives: fail, if_fail, while_success and ChoiceSet.Pick; the grammar combinators; try, catch, throw and defer; store and restore; timeout, hold and retry; multiple and shared inheritance, tagging and inner classes; interface cast and views; class fields; singleton and unique instances; operators and access checks.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.5 3.5.2.1 3.5.4.2 3.5.2.7 3.5.2.8 3.5.2.9 3.5.3.2 3.5.3.3 3.5.3.4 3.5.3.6
src: 2.8.2#68-74 2.8.15#126-135 2.1.13#43-46 2.8.3#742-752 2.8.3#775 2.8.3#781-784 2.3.1#652-654 2.3.1#356
limit: The list is the reading's and no derivation was run. While_success, defer, hold, shared inheritance, tagging, inner classes, singleton, unique and operators stand in no node and rest on the cited lines. The 2000 object-model thesis says tagging lacked its normalization mechanism, and the thesis marks singleton and unique not supported yet.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: To keep: one meaning per control word; both strengths of choice with an explicit commit; a reversibility declaration per state; a failure that carries a reason; the reference pair with the two-base call rule; attributes and parameters on every declaration; grammar rules as cells of the language; binary layout and value-level types.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.1
name: one-meaning-per-control-word
kind: finding
is: Give each control word one definition. Across the 2000 system and the three 2026 readers, fail, cut, choice, class, template, store and undo each have two to four meanings today, four for fail and for cut, and the re-entrant reading of choice must stay expressible.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.5.1.3 3.5.2.2 3.5.2.3 3.5.2.4 3.5.2.5 3.5.2.6 3.5.2.7 3.5.3.1 3.5.3.2
src: 2.8.13#525
limit: The reading counts two or three. Four for fail counts the 2000 machine mode, reader (a)'s throw node, reader (b)'s FAILED flag and reader (c)'s value nothing; four for cut counts the two 2000 descriptions separately. Store stands for the family save, mark, restore and discard.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.2
name: two-strengths-of-choice
kind: finding
is: Keep both strengths of choice and name them apart: first-that-answers, which commits at exit, and stay-open, which is re-entrant. Scoped choice is re-entrant choice plus an automatic commit, so one construct with an explicit commit, a scope rule for cut and its partner mark suffices, provided the default strength is stated.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.2.2 3.5.2.3 3.5.2.5
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.3
name: reversibility-declaration
kind: finding
is: Keep a reversibility declaration that can be attached to any state or effect: immutable and repointable, journaled, having an inverse (do, redo, undo), or irreversible. The 2026 body has mechanisms for the first two only and one sentence in a document for the irreversible case.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.2.6 3.5.2.7 3.5.2.10 1.7.8
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.4
name: failure-carries-a-reason
kind: finding
is: Keep a failure that can carry a reason, as a node acknowledgment or a thrown value, so that a typed catch and a backtrack walk with memory are one construct. Keep absence distinct from zero, empty and false in every position, and let every unwind to a recover point leave a reading.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.2.9 3.5.2.4 1.5 1.1
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.5
name: reference-pair-and-two-bases
kind: finding
is: Keep the reference as a (structure, behaviour) pair with the two-base call rule and cast as re-pairing, so that multiple inheritance by delegation, shared bases, tagging, detached interfaces and views are library patterns. A record with a class id cannot show the same data through a second interface without copying or wrapping.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.3.4 3.5.3.5
limit: No running reference for the pair or for delegation exists in either era.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.6
name: attributes-and-parameters-everywhere
kind: finding
is: Keep attributes on every declaration, user-extensible and readable at compile time and at run time, with a section form that applies a set to many members. Keep parameterised declarations at every site: blueprints, interfaces, recipes and grammar rules, with optional bounds, defaults and constants as parameters.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.3.6 3.5.3.1 3.5.4.1
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.7
name: grammar-rules-as-cells
kind: finding
is: Keep grammar rules as cells of the one language: a rule is a recipe with a pattern, an action and optionally an inverse; rules take arguments; a blueprint may carry named syntaxes whose captures bind its fields; the rule set may grow during a parse. Rules written with the language's own choice, fail and cut need no second interpreter.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.5.4.1 3.5.4.2 3.5.4.3 1.9.2
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.8.8
name: binary-layout-and-value-types
kind: finding
is: Keep binary layout declarations (binary types with size and mapping, struct classes, inline fields) and value-level types beyond comparison contracts. 2026 reader (b) parses binary type declarations and lists struct and inline as property words; no lowering of them to a layout was found, and reader (c)'s grammar and lowering lack the word binary.
status: inferred
conf: low
from: 3.5.3.6 3.5.3.1
src: 2.3.1#271-274 2.3.1#662 2.8.12#39 2.8.12#739 2.8.12#944 2.8.13 2.8.14 2.8.15
why: Value-level types keep overload resolution, coercion chains, strict fields and cast parameters expressible, and layout bears on a bootstrap that emits machine code.
limit: Not found means a word search on 2026-11-24: reader (b)'s lowering file has no line with BinaryType, binary, struct, inline, noobject or dynamic, and reader (c)'s grammar and lowering files have none with binary. Neither premise speaks of layout; the reading's own not found for struct and inline is a search of comment lines.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: What can go without losing expressiveness: mechanisms that are derivable (the separate exception channel; store and restore as words over immutable state), the 2000 compiler's fixed phases and operator tables, the text hop between grammar and nodes, and every reader beyond one.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.9.3
name: text-hop
kind: finding
is: Drop the text hop between grammar and nodes. In the 2026 build, strings are the seams between lowering stages and also the cache keys, so one edit invalidates a whole closure while the unit of meaning is the recipe.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.5.4.4
src: 2.8.19#8 2.8.19#26
limit: The old body measured its text printer at 15 microseconds a recipe against 116 for a node walker, so removing the hop alone does not shorten a cold build; the lever it names is a cache keyed on the recipe's content id.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.5.9.4
name: extra-readers
kind: finding
is: Drop every BML reader beyond one: reader (a), which erases types and cannot tell a failure from an exception, and the second statement walker beside the cursor grammar, which was already to be released so that new syntax lands once.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.5.1.3
at: 2026-11-24

